---
import { profile } from '../data/portfolio';
---

<section id="about" class="container-site py-20 md:py-28">
  <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,7fr)] md:gap-16">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">01 — About</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mb-4">Engineering, end to end.</h2>
      <p class="prose-body text-sm">
        Computer science student focused on building scalable backend systems and high-performance interfaces.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-body space-y-5 text-[1.02rem]">
      <p>
        I'm {profile.firstName}. I spend most of my time on the parts of a system users never see: APIs that stay
        fast under load, jobs that run reliably in the background, databases that don't become a bottleneck, and
        tooling that keeps development moving.
      </p>
      <p>
        My day-to-day is Go, Node.js, and Java on the backend, with TypeScript and React when the work needs an
        interface. I'm comfortable owning a feature from SQL migration to deployed service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Recently I built an automation tool that cut local development setup time roughly in half — the kind of
        problem I like most: slow, manual work turned into a fast, repeatable command. I run Linux (Arch, in case
        you were wondering) and I'm actively growing toward more distributed, production-focused engineering.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm">
        Currently learning: deeper distributed systems, Go concurrency in anger, and infrastructure that survives
        real traffic.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
